  "title": "Magnetic field along z",
  "spoken": "The magnetic field along z in the moving system is gamma times the difference: the stationary magnetic field along z, minus v times the stationary electric field along y divided by c squared.",
  "explanation": "The z component, with the opposite sign.",
  "review": "draft",
  "notation": "modern-pedagogical",
  "unitSystem": "si",
  "assumptions": [
    "The moving system moves along x at speed v relative to the stationary system, with |v| < c. Modern teaching notation: gamma is the paper's beta, c its V.",
    "Fields in empty space, in SI units; E is the electric field and B the magnetic field, with components along x, y and z."
  ],
